{
  "id": "individualized-education-program",
  "term": "individualized education program",
  "definition": "An individualized education program (IEP) is a special education plan developed through a school-based process under U.S. disability law for a student who may qualify for services. After referral, parent consent, and evaluation, the IEP meeting is used to decide eligibility and to set the student’s goals, services, and accommodations, with parents included and informed of their rights.",
